        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 73-year-old female patient, admitted on 28 November 2024 due to an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray confirming pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation, arterial blood gas analysis revealing hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia, and pulse oximetry monitoring throughout the stay. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. Treatment consisted of inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. The patient was discharged on 29 November 2024 in stable condition. We recommend continuation of her optimised inhaler regimen and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you have any questions.</div>"
            },
